course: dictionary
lesson: 1208
title: A bush that feeds butterflies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A buddleia is a noun, a name for a real plant. It is a bush with long, cone-shaped clusters of flowers in purple, white or pink. Another name for it is the butterfly bush, and it can also be spelled buddleja.
explain: Use the context to work out the meaning. «Buddleia, called the butterfly bush, is full of nectar and attracts many butterflies to a garden.» The words called the butterfly bush tell you the second name. Attracts means draws towards, so the butterflies come to the plant.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put butterfly bush in place of buddleia: «Butterfly bush, called the butterfly bush, is full of nectar...» It still makes sense, so both names mean the same plant. A dictionary tells you the plural is buddleias.
fact: A buddleia is also called the butterfly bush.
fact: Its flowers grow in long, cone-shaped clusters in purple, white or pink.
fact: Butterflies are drawn to a buddleia because it is full of nectar.
fact: In the UK, buddleias often grow on railway sides and old walls.
fact: Buddleias are loved by butterflies, but they can spread too much.
exercise: «Buddleia, called the butterfly bush, is full of nectar.» What is another name for a buddleia? | Railway bush | Nectar tree | *Butterfly bush | Garden wall
exercise: What shape are the flower clusters of a buddleia? | *Long and cone-shaped | Flat like a plate | Square and hard | Round like a ball
exercise: Which colours are the flowers of a buddleia? | Black and red | Blue and yellow only | Green and brown | *Purple, white or pink
test: Why do so many butterflies visit a buddleia? | Because it is made of stone | Because it has no flowers | Because it grows under the ground | *Because it is full of nectar
test: What does «attracts» mean in «attracts many butterflies to a garden»? | Forgets | Hides from | Pushes away | *Draws towards
exam: What is the plural of buddleia? | Buddleis | Buddlias | Buddleia's | *Buddleias
